  ],
  "text": "Squeeze the Earth down to the size of a marble and it becomes a black hole. Throw a ball hard enough and it leaves your hand. Harder still and it leaves the planet. That speed has a number. For Earth it is eleven kilometres every second. But squeeze the same mass into a smaller ball, and that number climbs. Squeeze it far enough and the number passes the speed of light. And nothing goes faster than light. So nothing ever gets back out. That edge is called the event horizon, and it only works one way. Fall in feet first, and your feet are pulled harder than your head. You would be drawn out into a thread. Astronomers really do call it spaghettification. But a black hole does not suck. Swap the Sun for one of the same mass. Earth's orbit would not change at all. We would simply freeze in the dark. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
